task_id: grpc__grpc-go-3361
category: Multi-SWE-bench Go
problem_statement_file: .benchmark/issue.md
repository:
  url: https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go.git
  base_commit: 648cf9b00e25b3af7839d6678a8fe319505c3b80
contexts:
  - small
interactive_followups:
  - "When round-robin clients lose their usable DNS endpoints, they need a way to refresh the resolver state instead of remaining stuck on failed addresses."
  - "Trace empty resolver updates through the shared base balancer. A resolver result with no addresses should request the ClientConn's existing backoff-based re-resolution, while normal address updates should stop that retry loop."
  - "In balancer/base, retain the latest resolver error separately from the latest connection error. For an empty address result, record a resolver error and return balancer.ErrBadResolverState; clear that resolver error after a successful resolution. When the aggregate state is TransientFailure, rebuild the picker with the available resolver and connection errors combined."
complexity:
  locality: 4
  context: 4
  ambiguity: 3
  composition: 4
  invariants: 5
  scale: 3
  staging: 5
